.TH HSH 1 "August 2026" "Holberton School" "Simple Shell Manual"
.SH NAME
hsh \- simple shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.br
.B echo
.I "command"
.B | ./hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
hsh is a simple shell program that has an interactive and a
non-interactive mode.
.PP
In interactive mode it prints the prompt
.B UZ$
and waits for a command.
In non-interactive mode it reads commands from standard input
and executes them without a prompt.
.PP
It tokenizes the input, checks if the command is a built-in,
resolves PATH when needed, and executes a command in a child process.
.SH BUILTINS
.TP
.B exit
Exits the shell with the last exit status.
.TP
.B env
Prints the current environment.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I main.c
Runs the simple shell.
.TP
.I main.h
Header with the function prototypes.
.TP
.I uz_tokenizeinput.c
Tokenizes the input.
.TP
.I uz_builtins.c
Checks if the command is a built-in and executes it.
.TP
.I uz_path.c
Gives the PATH for a command.
.TP
.I uz_handleexecution.c
Resolves PATH and makes fork.
.TP
.I uz_sh.c
Executes a command in a child process.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 if success, otherwise the status of the last command
(or 127 if the command is not found).
.SH EXAMPLES
Interactive mode:
.PP
.nf
$ ./hsh
UZ$ ls
AUTHORS  main.c  main.h  README.md  hsh
UZ$ env
UZ$ exit
$
.fi
.PP
Non-interactive mode:
.PP
.nf
$ echo "ls" | ./hsh
AUTHORS  main.c  main.h  README.md  hsh
$
.fi
